  "assumptions": [
    "All supplied material is purchased: purchase cost equals actual supply times normalized material price, not ordered amount.",
    "Stationary supplier order capacity is the W001-W168 positive-order 75th percentile; fulfillment and loss estimators differ by preregistered candidate.",
    "No claim is made about true external maximum capacity or weather-realized future performance.",
    "Nominal plan repeats for24weeks; initial inventory equals two target-production weeks. Stress recursively uses W169-W216 only; W217-W240 is excluded.",
    "Q2 uses conditional minimum cardinality, then purchase cost, then transport loss. Q3 preference uses declared C-min/A-max/purchase/loss lexicographic order, an interpretation of the underspecified tradeoff.",
    "Absolute transport and storage tariffs are missing; normalized purchase/loss objectives do not equal fully specified total monetary cost.",
    "Supplier and carrier tables share the company/week context; conditional routing combines their complete sets, not an observed supplier-carrier empirical crosswalk.",
    "Only derived24week plan CSVs are created; missing native Attachment A/B template conformance remains incomplete."
  ]
}
